  {
    "createdAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:41.640Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:41.640Z",
    "question": "What can the AI assistant inside the coach app do?",
    "answer": {
      "root": {
        "type": "root",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "direction": "ltr",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "direction": "ltr",
            "textFormat": 0,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "format": 0,
                "style": "",
                "mode": "normal",
                "detail": 0,
                "text": "It reads a client's profile, logged sessions, habit compliance and recent check-ins, then proposes the next adjustment to their workout or diet plan with the reasoning attached. It can also sweep your whole roster for clients who have gone quiet, dropped below a compliance threshold, or whose subscription is about to lapse. You review and approve everything it suggests.",
                "version": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "category": "getting-started",
    "order": 16,
    "featuredOnPages": [
      "faq"
    ],
    "_status": "published",
    "id": "6a9d3fe11ffc75efe99608e1"
  },
  {
    "createdAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:41.418Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T11:32:05.595Z",
    "question": "Does the AI change my clients' plans on its own?",
    "answer": {
      "root": {
        "type": "root",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "direction": "ltr",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "direction": "ltr",
            "textFormat": 0,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "format": 0,
                "style": "",
                "mode": "normal",
                "detail": 0,
                "text": "No. The AI drafts changes and explains its reasoning, but nothing reaches a client until you approve it. It cannot message your clients, cancel anyone, or push a plan change by itself. It does the assembling and the arithmetic — you stay the coach who decides.",
                "version": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "category": "getting-started",
    "order": 11,
    "featuredOnPages": [
      "faq",
      "home"
    ],
    "_status": "published",
    "id": "6a9d3fe11ffc75efe99608da"
  },
  {
    "createdAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:41.212Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T11:32:06.157Z",
    "question": "Can I connect Trainzilla to Claude, ChatGPT or another AI assistant?",
    "answer": {
      "root": {
        "type": "root",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "direction": "ltr",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "direction": "ltr",
            "textFormat": 0,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "format": 0,
                "style": "",
                "mode": "normal",
                "detail": 0,
                "text": "Yes. Trainzilla has a secure connector (MCP) that links your coach account to Claude and other assistants that support it. Once connected you can ask in plain language — \"which clients haven't checked in this week?\", \"recalculate macros for this client at 2g protein per kg\" — and the assistant works with your real client data. You authorise the connection yourself, it only ever acts as you, and every change it proposes is shown to you before anything is saved.",
                "version": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "category": "getting-started",
    "order": 14,
    "featuredOnPages": [
      "faq",
      "home"
    ],
    "_status": "published",
    "id": "6a9d3fe11ffc75efe99608d3"
  },
  {
    "createdAt": "2026-09-02T15:43:05.459Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:39.516Z",
    "question": "What do I need to start using Trainzilla?",
    "answer": {
      "root": {
        "type": "root",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "direction": "ltr",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "direction": "ltr",
            "textFormat": 0,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "format": 0,
                "style": "",
                "mode": "normal",
                "detail": 0,
                "text": "Just a phone or laptop with a browser — Trainzilla runs online, there is nothing for you to install. Your clients use the free Trainzilla mobile app to see their plan, log workouts, tick off habits and message you. For live video sessions you can use any call tool you already have (Zoom, Google Meet, WhatsApp); Trainzilla stores the link and handles the scheduling and reminders.",
                "version": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "category": "video-training",
    "order": 190,
    "featuredOnPages": [
      "faq"
    ],
    "_status": "published",
    "id": "6a98440936f85a38c0b83899"
  },
  {
    "createdAt": "2026-09-02T15:43:05.260Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T10:26:39.853Z",
    "question": "How do I conduct video training sessions?",
    "answer": {
      "root": {
        "type": "root",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "direction": "ltr",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "direction": "ltr",
            "textFormat": 0,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "format": 0,
                "style": "",
                "mode": "normal",
                "detail": 0,
                "text": "Schedule an online or in-person session in Trainzilla and attach your own video-call link — Zoom, Google Meet or whatever you already use. The session appears in your calendar and in the client's app with automatic reminders. Afterwards you mark attendance, so no-shows and patterns stay visible on the client's record.",
                "version": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
